== 3. the candidate as a CLI — the shape its own chart measures ==
provenance: no aarch64-linux release asset exists upstream (the published assets are macOS x2 and Windows x1), so this shape had to be built from the crates.io artifact. Upstream's own `[profile.release]` is the size-tuning pass the repo note records — `opt-level = "s", `lto = "fat", `codegen-units = 1`, `strip = "symbols"` — and that fat-LTO link was SIGKILLed by the kernel (OOM) **twice** on this 8 GiB box, once at cargo's default job count and once at `CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=1`, so the shipped profile is not buildable here at all. What the CLI rows below measured is therefore `cargo build --release --bin rho --locked` with `CARGO_PROFILE_RELEASE_LTO=thin`: every other release knob as upstream, one deviation named in the row, and a note that the fat-LTO build a user would download is a *different* artifact whose size this capture does not measure.
