The embedded program's own header says why there is no embedded-with-a-real-model arm here:
  rho-sdk 5.9.0 depends on serde, serde_json, thiserror, tokio, tracing, url, uuid — no
  HTTP client of any kind, and its only provider is `ScriptedProvider`, a test double.
  The model clients live in `rho-providers`, which is what composes a working agent.
  So embedding rho is a *crate composition* decision, not a dependency line, and the
  real-endpoint rows in this capture are the CLI's, which is that composition already
  built. Everything below measures the runtime, not the transport.

